hadiths[40]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1651.1","Yahya narrated to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Sa'id that he said: Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Hazm informed me that he seized a Nabatean who had stolen iron rings. He imprisoned him to cut his hand. 'Amrah bint 'Abd al-Rahman sent her mawla, Ummayyah, to him. Abu Bakr said: She came to me while I was among people and said, ""Your aunt 'Amrah says to you, O son of my sister: You seized a Nabatean for a trifle, it was mentioned to me, and you wanted to cut his hand?"" I said, ""Yes."" She said, ""'Amrah says to you: There is no cutting except for a quarter dinar or more."" Abu Bakr said: So I released the Nabatean. Malik said: The agreed ruling with us concerning the confession of slaves is that whoever confesses to something that incurs a hadd or corporal punishment on his body, his confession is valid against him, and he is not suspected of bringing this upon himself. But whoever confesses to something that entails a financial liability on his master, his confession is not valid against his master. Malik said: There is no cutting on a hired worker or a man who serves a people if they steal from them, because their condition is not that of a thief; their condition is that of a betrayer, and there is no cutting on a betrayer. Malik said concerning one who borrows an item and denies it: there is no cutting on him; it is like a man who has a debt on another and the other denies it — no cutting for the denial. Malik said: The agreed ruling with us concerning a thief found in a house having gathered the goods but not taken them out: there is no cutting on him. It is like a man who places wine before himself to drink but does not drink — no hadd on him. Like a man who sits with a woman intending to commit fornication but does not do it and does not consummate — no hadd on him either. Malik said: The agreed ruling with us is that there is no cutting in khulsa (stealthy taking without breaking security), whether the value reaches the cutting threshold or not."
"1651.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam that Jabir ibn Abdullah al-Ansari said"
"1652.1","Yahya related to me from Malik that he heard that Umar ibn al- Khattab said"
"1652.2","Yahya related to me from Malik that he heard that Umar ibn al- Khattab said"
"1653.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ayyub ibn Abi Tamim that Ibn Sirin said"
"1653.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ayyub ibn Abi Tamim that Ibn Sirin said"
"1654.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar wore garments dyed with red earth and dyed with saffron"
"1654.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar wore garments dyed with red earth and dyed with saffron"
"1655.1","It was narrated to me from Malik, from Ibn Shihab, that he was asked about the prescribed punishment for a slave concerning wine. He said: It has reached me that he receives half the prescribed punishment of a free person concerning wine. And that Umar ibn al-Khattab, Uthman ibn Affan, and Abdullah ibn Umar had flogged their slaves half the prescribed punishment of a free person concerning wine."
"1655.2","It was narrated to me from Malik, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, will not look on the Day of Resurrection at him who drags his garment out of arrogance."
"1656.1","Malik related to me from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that A'isha the wife of the Prophet"
"1656.2","Malik related to me from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that A'isha the wife of the Prophet"
"1657.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Alqama ibn Abi Alqama that his mother said"
"1657.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Alqama ibn Abi Alqama that his mother said"
